=== meta ===
rule: EXPECTATION_DEFINITION_CHANGED
title: Editing the input column while appending a row is still not an oracle edit
note: Research E-08b paired control for param_row_cell_edit_appended_pos:
note2: the row-keyed comparison must not read a changed input as a changed
note3: expectation (the pairing it had is simply no longer tested). The
note4: frozen expectation_parametrize_input_neg pins the same contract
note5: without the appended row.
note6: reclassified 2026-09-21 (issue #93 contract decision, estate T-436,
note7: DECISIONS D-060): the appended row no longer masks the relabeling —
note8: SUBJECT_INPUT_CHANGED pairs the vanished input with the arriving
note9: row that keeps its answer. EXPECTATION_DEFINITION_CHANGED stays
note10: silent, which remains this control's point.
=== before: tests/test_billing.py ===
import pytest

from billing import invoice_total


@pytest.mark.parametrize(
    "items,expected",
    [
        ([50.0, 50.0], 105.0),
        ([10.0], 10.5),
    ],
)
def test_invoice_total_applies_tax(items, expected):
    assert invoice_total(items, 0.05) == expected
=== after: tests/test_billing.py ===
import pytest

from billing import invoice_total


@pytest.mark.parametrize(
    "items,expected",
    [
        ([60.0, 40.0], 105.0),
        ([10.0], 10.5),
        ([1.0, 1.0], 2.1),
    ],
)
def test_invoice_total_applies_tax(items, expected):
    assert invoice_total(items, 0.05) == expected
